{"name":"Voyage","hex":"#719ca4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"voyage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long journey, especially by ship.","A written account of a journey or travel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To go on a long journey."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/voyage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sterling Hayden","blocks":[{"text":"Sterling Walter Hayden was an American actor. A leading man for most of his career, he specialized in Westerns and film noir throughout the 1950s, in films such as John Huston's The Asphalt Jungle (1950), Nicholas Ray's Johnny Guitar (1954), and Stanley Kubrick's The Killing (1956). In the 1960s, he became noted for supporting roles, perhaps most memorably as General Jack D. Ripper in Kubrick's Dr. Strangelove or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Bomb (1964)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Sterling_Hayden_1953_Alt_Edit.jpg/330px-Sterling_Hayden_1953_Alt_Edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sterling_Hayden"},{"title":"Voyage (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Voyage is a 1996 hard science fiction novel by British author Stephen Baxter. The book depicts a crewed mission to Mars as it might have been in another timeline, one where John F. Kennedy survived the assassination attempt on him on 22 November 1963. Voyage won a Sidewise Award for Alternate History, and was nominated for the Arthur C. Clarke Award in 1997."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0d/Voyage_Stephen_Baxter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voyage_(novel)"},{"title":"Voyage (ABBA album)","blocks":[{"text":"Voyage is the ninth and final studio album by the Swedish pop group ABBA, released on 5 November 2021. With ten songs written by Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus, it is the group's first album of new material in forty years, following The Visitors (1981). The album was supported by the dual single release of \"I Still Have Faith in You\" and \"Don't Shut Me Down\", released alongside the album announcement on 2 September 2021. \"Just a Notion\" was issued as the third single on 22 October 2021, followed by the fourth single \"Little Things\" on 3 December. A digital concert residency in support of the album, ABBA Voyage, opened in London on 27 May 2022."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e0/ABBA_-_Voyage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voyage_(ABBA_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Photo_of_Sterling_Hayden_Wearing_a_Hawely_Pith_Helmet.jpg/500px-Photo_of_Sterling_Hayden_Wearing_a_Hawely_Pith_Helmet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Photo_of_Sterling_Hayden_Wearing_a_Hawely_Pith_Helmet.jpg/500px-Photo_of_Sterling_Hayden_Wearing_a_Hawely_Pith_Helmet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hayden in his Marine Corps uniform at Parris Island c. January 1943","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhoto_of_Sterling_Hayden_Wearing_a_Hawely_Pith_Helmet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Hayden-Asphalt.jpg/500px-Hayden-Asphalt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Hayden-Asphalt.jpg/1280px-Hayden-Asphalt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Hayden-Asphalt.jpg/500px-Hayden-Asphalt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Publicity photo of Hayden from The Asphalt Jungle, 1950","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHayden-Asphalt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Sterling_Hayden_1947_crop.jpg/330px-Sterling_Hayden_1947_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Sterling_Hayden_1947_crop.jpg/330px-Sterling_Hayden_1947_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hayden as a member of the Committee for the First Amendment, October 1, 1947","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASterling_Hayden_1947_crop.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sterling_Hayden_in_The_Killing.png/500px-Sterling_Hayden_in_The_Killing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sterling_Hayden_in_The_Killing.png/1280px-Sterling_Hayden_in_The_Killing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Sterling_Hayden_in_The_Killing.png/500px-Sterling_Hayden_in_The_Killing.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sterling Hayden in The Killing","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASterling_Hayden_in_The_Killing.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Dr._Strangelove_-_Ripper_and_Mandrake.png/500px-Dr._Strangelove_-_Ripper_and_Mandrake.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Dr._Strangelove_-_Ripper_and_Mandrake.png/500px-Dr._Strangelove_-_Ripper_and_Mandrake.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sterling Hayden with Peter Sellers in Dr. Strangelove","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADr._Strangelove_-_Ripper_and_Ma